[186.476977, "o", "362:Except as provided in subsection (b), for purposes of this subtitle, the term \"taxable income\" means gross income minus the deductions allowed by this chapter (other than the standard deduction).\r\n368:    (1) the standard deduction, and\r\n378:    Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"standard deduction\" means the sum of-\r\n380:        (A) the basic standard deduction, and\r\n382:        (B) the additional standard deduction.\r\n384:    (2) Basic standard deduction\r\n386:    For purposes of paragraph (1), the basic standard deduction is-\r\n398:    (3) Additional standard deduction for aged and blind\r\n400:    For purposes of paragraph (1), the additional standard deduction is the sum of each additional amount to which the taxpayer is entitled under subsection (f).\r\n402:    (5) Limitation on basic standard deduction in the case of certain dependents\r\n404:    In the case of an individual with respect to whom a deduction under section 151 is allowable to another taxpayer for a taxable year beginni"]
[186.477116, "o", "ng in the calendar year in which the individual's taxable year begins, the basic standard deduction applicable to such individual for such individual's taxable year shall not exceed the greater of-\r\n410:    (6) Certain individuals, etc., not eligible for standard deduction\r\n420:    the standard deduction shall be zero.\r\n"]
