[1234.468107, "i", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt << 'EOF'\n## Statute\n\n**§1. Tax imposed - Married individuals filing separate returns**\nLines 44-54 of statute.txt:\n\"There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every married individual (as defined in section 7703) who does not make a single return jointly with his spouse, a tax determined in accordance with the following:\n    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $18,450;\n    (ii) $2,767.50, plus 28% of the excess over $18,450 if the taxable income is over $18,450 but not over $44,575;\n    (iii) $10,082.50, plus 31% of the excess over $44,575 if the taxable income is over $44,575 but not over $70,000;\n    (iv) $17,964.25, plus 36% of the excess over $70,000 if the taxable income is over $70,000 but not over $125,000;\n    (v) $37,764.25, plus 39.6% of the excess over $125,000 if the taxable income is over $125,000\"\n\n**§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions**\nLines 53-65 of statute.txt:\n\"(a) Allowance of deductions\nIn the case of an indivi"]
[1234.468266, "i", "dual, the exemptions provided by this section shall be allowed as deductions in computing taxable income.\n\n(b) Taxpayer and spouse\nAn exemption of the exemption amount for the taxpayer; and an additional exemption of the exemption amount for the spouse of the taxpayer if a joint return is not made by the taxpayer and his spouse, and if the spouse, for the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins, has no gross income and is not the dependent of another taxpayer.\n\n(c) Additional exemption for dependents\nAn exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year.\"\n\n**§151(d)(1). Exemption amount**\nLines 69-71 of statute.txt:\n\"(1) In general\nExcept as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\"\n\n**§151(d)(3)(B). Phaseout - Applicable percentage**\nLines 86-88 of statute.txt:\n\"For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term \"applicable percentage\" means 2 percentage points for e"]
[1234.46831, "o", "cat > /app/output/answer.txt << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.468321, "i", "ach $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting \"$1,250\" for \"$2,500\". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.\"\n\n**§152. Dependent defined**\nLines 95-142 of statute.txt:\n\"(a) In general\nFor purposes of this subtitle, the term \"dependent\" means:\n    (1) a qualifying child, or\n    (2) a qualifying relative.\n\n(c) Qualifying child\nFor purposes of this section:\n    (1) In general\n    The term \"qualifying child\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual:\n        (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\n        (B) who has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year,\n        (C) who meets the age requirements of paragraph (3), and\n        (E) who has not "]
[1234.468357, "o", "dual, the exemptions provided by this section shall be allowed as deductions in computing taxable income.\r\n\r\n(b) Taxpayer and spouse\r\nAn exemption of the exemption amount for the taxpayer; and an additional exemption of the exemption amount for the spouse of the taxpayer if a joint return is not made by the taxpayer and his spouse, and if the spouse, for the calendar yea"]
[1234.468409, "i", "filed a joint return (other than only for a claim of refund) with the individual's spouse for the taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins.\n    (2) Relationship\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(A), an individual bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in this paragraph if such individual is:\n        (A) a child of the taxpayer or a descendant of such a child, or\n        (B) a brother, sister, stepbrother, or stepsister of the taxpayer or a descendant of any such relative.\n    (3) Age requirements\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(C), an individual meets the requirements of this paragraph if such individual is younger than the taxpayer claiming such individual as a qualifying child and is less than 25 years old at the end of the taxable year.\"\n\n**§162(c)(6)(A). Certain individuals not eligible for standard deduction**\nLines 412-414 of statute.txt:\n\"In the case of:\n    (A) a married individual filing a separate return where either spouse itemizes dedu"]
[1234.468454, "o", "r in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins, has no gross income and is not the dependent of another taxpayer.\r\n\r\n(c) Additional exemption for dependents\r\nAn exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year.\"\r\n\r\n**§151(d)(1). Exemption amount**\r\nLines 69-71 of statute.txt:\r\n\"(1) In general\r\nExcept as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\"\r\n\r\n**§151(d)(3)(B). Phaseout - Applicable percentage**\r\nLines 86-88 of statute.txt:\r\n\"For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term \"applicable percentage\" means 2 percentage points for e"]
[1234.468478, "i", "ctions,\n    (B) a nonresident alien individual, or\n    (D) an estate or trust, common trust fund, or partnership,\nthe standard deduction shall be zero.\"\n\n**§68. Overall limitation on itemized deductions**\nLines 475-479 of statute.txt:\n\"(a) General rule\nIn the case of an individual whose adjusted gross income exceeds the applicable amount, the amount of the itemized deductions otherwise allowable for the taxable year shall be reduced by the lesser of:\n    (1) 3 percent of the excess of adjusted gross income over the applicable amount, or\n    (2) 80 percent of the amount of the itemized deductions otherwise allowable for such taxable year.\"\n\n**§68(b)(1)(D). Applicable amount**\nLines 493-494 of statute.txt:\n\"(D) 1/2 the amount applicable under subparagraph (A) in the case of a married individual filing a separate return.\"\n\n**§7703. Determination of marital status**\nLines 516-518 of statute.txt:\n\"(a) General rule\n    (1) the determination of whether an individual is married shall be made as of the close of his"]
[1234.468524, "o", "ach $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting \"$1,250\" for \"$2,500\". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.\"\r\n\r\n**§152. Dependent defined**\r\nLines 95-142 of statute.txt:\r\n\"(a) In general\r\nFor purposes of this subtitle, the term \"dependent\" means:\r\n    (1) a qualifying child, or\r\n    (2) a qualifying relative.\r\n\r\n(c) Qualifying child\r\nFor purposes of this section:\r\n    (1) In general\r\n    The term \"qualifying child\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual:\r\n        (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\r\n        (B) who has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year,\r\n        (C) who meets the age requirements of paragraph (3), and\r\n        "]
[1234.46855, "i", " taxable year; except that if his spouse dies during his taxable year such determination shall be made as of the time of such death; and\n    (2) an individual legally separated from his spouse under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance shall not be considered as married.\"\n\n## Reasoning\n\n**Step 1: Determine Alice's filing status**\n- Alice is married (married Jan 12, 2016, §7703(a)(1))\n- Alice does not file a joint return (given in facts)\n- Filing status: Married Filing Separately (§1(d))\n\n**Step 2: Determine standard deduction**\n- Alice itemizes deductions of $100,206 (given in facts)\n- Under §162(c)(6)(A), a married individual filing separately where either spouse itemizes has standard deduction of $0\n- Standard deduction = $0\n\n**Step 3: Determine personal exemptions**\n- Alice's exemption: $2,000 (§151(b))\n- Husband's exemption: $2,000 (§151(b) - no joint return, no gross income, not dependent of another)\n- Bob's exemption: $2,000 (§151(c) - qualifying child under §152(c))\n  - Relationship: B"]
[1234.468571, "o", "(E) who has not filed a joint return (other than only for a claim of refund) with the individual's spouse for the taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins.\r\n    (2) Relationship\r\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(A), an individual bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in this paragraph if such individual is:\r\n        (A) a child of the taxpayer or a descendant of such a child, or\r\n        (B) a brother, sister, stepbrother, or step"]
[1234.468595, "i", "ob is Alice's brother (§152(c)(2)(B))\n  - Same principal place of abode: Bob \"has always lived at his parents' place\" (§152(c)(1)(B))\n  - Age: Born Jan 31, 2014, so 2 years old in 2016, less than 25 (§152(c)(3))\n  - No joint return filed by Bob (§152(c)(1)(E))\n- Total exemptions before phaseout: $6,000\n\n**Step 4: Calculate exemption phaseout (§151(d)(3))**\n- Applicable amount for MFS: $150,000 (§68(b)(1)(D) = 1/2 × $300,000)\n- Alice's AGI: $567,192 (given in facts)\n- Excess AGI: $567,192 - $150,000 = $417,192\n- Increments of $1,250: ceiling($417,192 / $1,250) = 334\n- Phaseout percentage: min(100, 334 × 2) = 100%\n- Exemptions after phaseout: $6,000 × (100 - 100)% = $0\n\n**Step 5: Calculate itemized deduction limitation (§68)**\n- 3% of excess AGI: 0.03 × $417,192 = $12,515.76\n- 80% of itemized deductions: 0.80 × $100,206 = $80,164.80\n- Lesser amount: $12,515.76\n- Net itemized deductions: $100,206 - $12,515.76 = $87,690.24\n\n**Step 6: Calculate taxable income**\n- Taxable income = AGI - net itemized ded"]
[1234.468626, "o", "sister of the taxpayer or a descendant of any such relative.\r\n    (3) Age requirements\r\n    For purposes of paragraph (1)(C), an individual meets the requirements of this paragraph if such individual is younger than the taxpayer claiming such individual as a qualifying child and is less than 25 years old at the end of the taxable year.\"\r\n\r\n**§162(c)(6)(A). Certain individuals not eligible for standard deduction**\r\nLines 412-414 of statute.txt:\r\n\"In the case "]
[1234.468644, "i", "uctions - exemptions\n- Taxable income = $567,192 - $87,690.24 - $0 = $479,501.76\n\n**Step 7: Calculate tax (§1(d)(v))**\n- Taxable income $479,501.76 exceeds $125,000\n- Tax = $37,764.25 + 39.6% × ($479,501.76 - $125,000)\n- Tax = $37,764.25 + 0.396 × $354,501.76\n- Tax = $37,764.25 + $140,382.69776 = $178,146.94776\n- Tax rounded to nearest dollar: $178,147\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 178147\nEOF\n"]
[1234.468681, "o", "of:\r\n    (A) a married individual filing a separate return where either spouse itemizes deductions,\r\n    (B) a nonresident alien i\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.468705, "o", "## Statute\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.468733, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.468759, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.468897, "o", "**§1. Tax imposed - Married individuals filing separate returns**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.468925, "o", "> "]
[1234.468965, "o", "Lines 44-54 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.468974, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.468992, "o", "> "]
[1234.469476, "o", "\"There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every married individual (as defined in section 7703) who does not make a single return jointly with his spouse, a tax determined in accordance with the following:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.46954, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.469667, "o", "    (i) 15% of taxable income if the taxable income is not over $18,450;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.469674, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.469695, "o", "> "]
[1234.469967, "o", "    (ii) $2,767.50, plus 28% of the excess over $18,450 if the taxable income is over $18,450 but not over $44,575;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.469974, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.470327, "o", "    (iii) $10,082.50, plus 31% of the excess over $44,575 if the taxable income is over $44,575 but not over $70,000;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.470586, "o", "    (iv) $17,964.25, plus 36% of the excess over $70,000 if the taxable income is over $70,000 but not over $125,000;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.47071, "o", "    (v) $37,764.25, plus 39.6% of the excess over $125,000 if the taxable income is over $125,000\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.470797, "o", "**§151. Allowance of deductions for personal exemptions**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.470818, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.470843, "o", "> "]
[1234.470889, "o", "Lines 53-65 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.470913, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.470937, "o", "> "]
[1234.470979, "o", "\"(a) Allowance of deductions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.471005, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.47103, "o", "> "]
[1234.471245, "o", "In the case of an individual, the exemptions provided by this section shall be allowed as deductions in computing taxable income.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[1234.471269, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.47129, "o", "> "]
[1234.47133, "o", "(b) Taxpayer and spouse\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.471355, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.471377, "o", "> "]
[1234.471987, "o", "An exemption of the exemption amount for the taxpayer; and an additional exemption of the exemption amount for the spouse of the taxpayer if a joint return is not made by the taxpayer and his spouse, and if the spouse, for the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins, has no gross income and is not the dependent of another taxpayer.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\ra joint return (given in "]
[1234.472009, "o", "facts)\r\n- Filing status: Married Filing Sep\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\ra"]
[1234.472064, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.472133, "o", "(c) Additional exemption for dependents\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.47216, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.472186, "o", "> "]
[1234.47252, "o", "An exemption of the exemption amount for each individual who is a dependent (as defined in section 152) of the taxpayer for the taxable year.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.472548, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.472573, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.472641, "o", "**§151(d)(1). Exemption amount**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.472667, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.472692, "o", "> "]
[1234.472731, "o", "Lines 69-71 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.472754, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.472782, "o", "> "]
[1234.472808, "o", "\"(1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.472834, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.473047, "o", "Except as otherwise provided in this subsection, the term \"exemption amount\" means $2,000.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.473069, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.473091, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.473227, "o", "**§151(d)(3)(B). Phaseout - Applicable percentage**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.47325, "o", "> "]
[1234.473312, "o", "Lines 86-88 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.473334, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.473347, "o", "> "]
[1234.474506, "o", "\"For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term \"applicable percentage\" means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer's adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b). In the case of a married individual filing a separate return, the preceding sentence shall be applied by substituting \"$1,250\" for \"$2,500\". In no event shall the applicable percentage exceed 100 percent.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.474531, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.474552, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.474619, "o", "**§152. Dependent defined**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.474646, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.474713, "o", "Lines 95-142 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.474739, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.474766, "o", "> "]
[1234.474793, "o", "\"(a) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.474816, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.474937, "o", "For purposes of this subtitle, the term \"dependent\" means:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.474963, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.47499, "o", "> "]
[1234.475032, "o", "    (1) a qualifying child, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475063, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.475086, "o", "> "]
[1234.475136, "o", "    (2) a qualifying relative.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475161, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475185, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.47522, "o", "(c) Qualifying child\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475243, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.475264, "o", "> "]
[1234.47531, "o", "For purposes of this section:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475336, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.475378, "o", "    (1) In general\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475399, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.475425, "o", "> "]
[1234.475653, "o", "    The term \"qualifying child\" means, with respect to any taxpayer for any taxable year, an individual:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475671, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.475694, "o", "> "]
[1234.475865, "o", "        (A) who bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in paragraph (2),\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.475881, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.475902, "o", "> "]
[1234.476173, "o", "        (B) who has the same principal place of abode as the taxpayer for more than one-half of such taxable year,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.476197, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.476358, "o", "        (C) who meets the age requirements of paragraph (3), and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.476383, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.476402, "o", "> "]
[1234.476917, "o", "        (E) who has not filed a joint return (other than only for a claim of refund) with the individual's spouse for the taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which the taxable year of the taxpayer begins.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.476936, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.476958, "o", "> "]
[1234.476987, "o", "    (2) Relationship\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.477, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.477025, "o", "> "]
[1234.477367, "o", "    For purposes of paragraph (1)(A), an individual bears a relationship to the taxpayer described in this paragraph if such individual is:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.477389, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.477412, "o", "> "]
[1234.477526, "o", "        (A) a child of the taxpayer or a descendant of such a child, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.477548, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.477692, "o", "        (B) a brother, sister, stepbrother, or stepsister of the taxpayer or a descendant of any such relative.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.477714, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.477752, "o", "> "]
[1234.477772, "o", "    (3) Age requirements\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.47809, "o", "    For purposes of paragraph (1)(C), an individual meets the requirements of this paragraph if such individual is younger than the taxpayer claiming such individual as a qualifying child and is less than 25 years old at the end of the taxable year.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478139, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478164, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.478222, "o", "**§162(c)(6)(A). Certain individuals not eligible for standard deduction**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478248, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.478275, "o", "> "]
[1234.478296, "o", "Lines 412-414 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.478317, "o", "> "]
[1234.478334, "o", "\"In the case of:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478353, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.478463, "o", "    (A) a married individual filing a separate return where either spouse itemizes deductions,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478488, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.478534, "o", "    (B) a nonresident alien individual, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478558, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.478576, "o", "> "]
[1234.478633, "o", "    (D) an estate or trust, common trust fund, or partnership,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478657, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.478684, "o", "> "]
[1234.478711, "o", "the standard deduction shall be zero.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478735, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478761, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.478804, "o", "**§68. Overall limitation on itemized deductions**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478829, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.478854, "o", "> "]
[1234.478879, "o", "Lines 475-479 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.478904, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.47893, "o", "\"(a) General rule\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.478956, "o", "> "]
[1234.479184, "o", "In the case of an individual whose adjusted gross income exceeds the applicable amount, the amount of the itemized deductions otherwise allowable for the taxable year shall be reduced by the lesser of:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.479193, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.479316, "o", "    (1) 3 percent of the excess of adjusted gross income over the applicable amount, or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.479352, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.479466, "o", "    (2) 80 percent of the amount of the itemized deductions otherwise allowable for such taxable year.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.479493, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.479511, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.47955, "o", "**§68(b)(1)(D). Applicable amount**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.479576, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.479601, "o", "> "]
[1234.479626, "o", "Lines 493-494 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.479652, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.479776, "o", "\"(D) 1/2 the amount applicable under subparagraph (A) in the case of a married individual filing a separate return.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.479796, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.479821, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.47987, "o", "**§7703. Determination of marital status**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.47989, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.479913, "o", "> "]
[1234.479936, "o", "Lines 516-518 of statute.txt:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.479956, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.479979, "o", "\"(a) General rule\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.480001, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.480292, "o", "    (1) the determination of whether an individual is married shall be made as of the close of his taxable year; except that if his spouse dies during his taxable year such determination shall be made as of the time of such death; and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.480305, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.480498, "o", "    (2) an individual legally separated from his spouse under a decree of divorce or of separate maintenance shall not be considered as married.\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.480506, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.480536, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.480564, "o", "## Reasoning\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.480585, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.480602, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.480644, "o", "**Step 1: Determine Alice's filing status**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.480671, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.480698, "o", "> "]
[1234.480735, "o", "- Alice is married (married Jan 12, 2016, §7703(a)(1))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.48076, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.480784, "o", "> "]
[1234.480823, "o", "- Alice does not file a joint return (given in facts)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.480849, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.480874, "o", "> "]
[1234.480909, "o", "- Filing status: Married Filing Separately (§1(d))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.480927, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.480952, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.480981, "o", "> "]
[1234.481009, "o", "**Step 2: Determine standard deduction**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.481029, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.481094, "o", "- Alice itemizes deductions of $100,206 (given in facts)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.481118, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.481146, "o", "> "]
[1234.481268, "o", "- Under §162(c)(6)(A), a married individual filing separately where either spouse itemizes has standard deduction of $0\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.481292, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.481318, "o", "> "]
[1234.481346, "o", "- Standard deduction = $0\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.48137, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.481411, "o", "**Step 3: Determine personal exemptions**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.481432, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.48146, "o", "> "]
[1234.481488, "o", "- Alice's exemption: $2,000 (§151(b))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.481512, "o", "> "]
[1234.481631, "o", "- Husband's exemption: $2,000 (§151(b) - no joint return, no gross income, not dependent of another)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.481657, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.481739, "o", "- Bob's exemption: $2,000 (§151(c) - qualifying child under §152(c))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.48177, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.481794, "o", "> "]
[1234.481833, "o", "  - Relationship: Bob is Alice's brother (§152(c)(2)(B))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.481863, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.481975, "o", "  - Same principal place of abode: Bob \"has always lived at his parents' place\" (§152(c)(1)(B))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.481999, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.482103, "o", "  - Age: Born Jan 31, 2014, so 2 years old in 2016, less than 25 (§152(c)(3))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482126, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482155, "o", "> "]
[1234.482186, "o", "  - No joint return filed by Bob (§152(c)(1)(E))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482211, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.482262, "o", "- Total exemptions before phaseout: $6,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482282, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482306, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.482368, "o", "**Step 4: Calculate exemption phaseout (§151(d)(3))**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482394, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482416, "o", "> "]
[1234.482479, "o", "- Applicable amount for MFS: $150,000 (§68(b)(1)(D) = 1/2 × $300,000)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482488, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.48252, "o", "> "]
[1234.482551, "o", "- Alice's AGI: $567,192 (given in facts)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482577, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482603, "o", "> "]
[1234.482628, "o", "- Excess AGI: $567,192 - $150,000 = $417,192\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482652, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482674, "o", "> "]
[1234.482721, "o", "- Increments of $1,250: ceiling($417,192 / $1,250) = 334\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482745, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482763, "o", "> "]
[1234.482802, "o", "- Phaseout percentage: min(100, 334 × 2) = 100%\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482827, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482853, "o", "> "]
[1234.482897, "o", "- Exemptions after phaseout: $6,000 × (100 - 100)% = $0\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.482918, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.482944, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.483008, "o", "**Step 5: Calculate itemized deduction limitation (§68)**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483016, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.48304, "o", "> "]
[1234.483097, "o", "- 3% of excess AGI: 0.03 × $417,192 = $12,515.76\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483127, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.483152, "o", "> "]
[1234.483194, "o", "- 80% of itemized deductions: 0.80 × $100,206 = $80,164.80\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483228, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.483273, "o", "- Lesser amount: $12,515.76\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483322, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.483409, "o", "- Net itemized deductions: $100,206 - $12,515.76 = $87,690.24\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483433, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.483454, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.483472, "o", "> "]
[1234.4835, "o", "**Step 6: Calculate taxable income**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483527, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.483551, "o", "> "]
[1234.4836, "o", "- Taxable income = AGI - net itemized deductions - exemptions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483622, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.483646, "o", "> "]
[1234.483699, "o", "- Taxable income = $567,192 - $87,690.24 - $0 = $479,501.76\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483721, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.483747, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.483781, "o", "**Step 7: Calculate tax (§1(d)(v))**\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483806, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.483836, "o", "> "]
[1234.483859, "o", "- Taxable income $479,501.76 exceeds $125,000\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483884, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.483909, "o", "> "]
[1234.48395, "o", "- Tax = $37,764.25 + 39.6% × ($479,501.76 - $125,000)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.483978, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.484005, "o", "> "]
[1234.484027, "o", "- Tax = $37,764.25 + 0.396 × $354,501.76\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.484051, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.484124, "o", "- Tax = $37,764.25 + $140,382.69776 = $178,146.94776\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.484147, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.484174, "o", "> "]
[1234.484198, "o", "- Tax rounded to nearest dollar: $178,147\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.484218, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[1234.48424, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.484263, "o", "## Answer\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1234.484288, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1234.484313, "o", "Answer: 178147\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
